{"posts":[{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_1","t":"Hydra\n\nHey there this is Hydra! this is my homework for spotting and drawing FL's - flag limits.\n\nNeed you comments and advises for them. thank you","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1","p":1,"im":[],"m":1},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_2","t":"Hydra\n\nAll right this is my first post drill on FL, well let's see. Please have a look and advise me if I'm wrong. regards","a":"—","d":"","n":"#2","p":1,"im":["94343e04f091342a904067dd44c537582e1de527"],"m":2},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_3","t":"Hydra\n\nHere we are on m1 and we have a well respected SR flip here in this pic 1\n\nand this is my FL highlighted which is afterwards consumed and move upwards","a":"—","d":"","n":"#3","p":1,"im":["a60b13937680571b4cdb1ab9581a4d65193ab565","2a6268056d088a80f356db4dbc090151c43aa876"],"m":3},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_4","t":"Hydra\n\nanother one...","a":"—","d":"","n":"#4","p":1,"im":["02b8e6afdd05450ff7dc8d987ec3282467911ad5"],"m":4},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_5","t":"Hydra","a":"—","d":"","n":"#5","p":1,"im":["5450a6e174a580a0ed5795557894ffed226cd6f9"],"m":5},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_6","t":"Enkim\n\nHi Hydra - here are my notes - hope it will help you. Enkim","a":"—","d":"","n":"#6","p":1,"im":["649d0ca2a8490d042cc3f934236a7d8d6c5e1729","3a8f9755e30af4ab4fdbc893b1203a43128c9c15"],"m":6},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_7","t":"Hydra","a":"—","d":"","n":"#7","p":1,"im":["9ddd982078f9f8e55192398bc42830a8458b4cda"],"m":7},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_8","t":"Hydra\n\nHi Enkim thanks for replying. Brother I have two questions in my mind. first is if we spot any FL how can we know how far flag is expended and my second question is how to spot Lower flags and Upper Flags?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#8","p":1,"im":["58d982162679efa9c49a1e3d37929389bf235d99"],"m":8},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_9","t":"Hydra\n\nI'm confusing here for instance if we spot flag and draw our rectangle on it. What will be our flag see picture below. i have drawn 3 black square and which is correct flag area among them?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#9","p":1,"im":["ebec13b0b951bddc84af609a8c9594776c505c91"],"m":9},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_10","t":"Enkim\n\nFL is no more when the price breaks its edge and makes an engulf. Then new FL is formed after price do its retrace and hit its target (another FL in opposite direction). If price does not engulf FL, then it is valid and can be valid for many years till the price comes to it again. Try to be very precise in drawing rectangles, because you need to see when it is engulfed. UPL and LFL are the most important FLs because they can hold the price, and you can chain them if you draw them correctly and very well use them to predict the future bounce. As for your last picture, i didnt look at it closer but if you want to draw FL after break of that low (or FL low was reacting to) the correct one is this:","a":"—","d":"","n":"#10","p":1,"im":["3c99cd11e11b00be718bc56abe73699a5ebb2970"],"m":10},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_11","t":"Hydra\n\nBro I'm still confused can you show me in diagram or illustrate it what is FL and what is UFL LFL? i will be thankful to you","a":"—","d":"","n":"#11","p":1,"im":[],"m":11},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_12","t":"einrikr\n\nThis diagram is always very helpful.\n\nUpper Flag Limits (UFL) keep price down and Lower Flag Limits (LFL) keep price up.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#12","p":1,"im":[],"m":12},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_13","t":"Hydra\n\nThanks for guiding me bro. I will post more charts. I was confused with terms also. i thought UFL means Upper Flag and LFL means lower flag","a":"—","d":"","n":"#13","p":1,"im":[],"m":13},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_14","t":"Hydra\n\neinrikr wrote: This diagram is always very helpful.\n\nUpper Flag Limits (UFL) keep price down and Lower Flag Limits (LFL) keep price up.\n\nBro can you post some examples from your charts. I would like to see. thank you once again","a":"—","d":"","n":"#14","p":1,"im":["242bf6f8ca9ea7e0f524636c2509b43d09089c1d"],"m":14},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_15","t":"Hydra\n\nBro is that correct? Blue box is HTF UFL and HTF LFL and red box is LTF FL","a":"—","d":"","n":"#15","p":1,"im":["66d60a739c6ef6e9aa4e69d4c5745ff1a27c021a"],"m":15},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_16","t":"Hydra\n\ncan any one answer this question? Im really confused with UFL and LFL","a":"—","d":"","n":"#16","p":1,"im":["1a4115698d6d4b964271f62b902ac9727a936951"],"m":16},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_17","t":"Hiya.\n\nHave you been through the entire Flag Limit thread yet? If not, I'd advise you to do so. LFL = Lower Flag Limit UFL = Upper Flag Limit They will always overlap each other\n\nWasher\n\nfind\n\n14517","a":"—","d":"","n":"#17","p":1,"im":[],"m":17},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_18","t":"Hydra\n\nThanks Sir ifmyante!!! I have read 10 pages and now I'm going to post my FL's again","a":"—","d":"","n":"#18","p":1,"im":[],"m":18},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_19","t":"Hydra\n\nFirst we have this m15 chart\n\nthen I went to m1 and found clear FL's here","a":"—","d":"","n":"#19","p":1,"im":["06273ba95f60c5c7dce79b52834cb056e64f7909","ad23ad5e2a9af2e52bb1e79d8236dc79b29acd45"],"m":19},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_20","t":"Hydra\n\nHere we have m15 of usdjpy, another example","a":"—","d":"","n":"#20","p":1,"im":["e1ad50faa71df409f6822aed6084e53c9b5f15c0"],"m":20},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_21","t":"Hydra","a":"—","d":"","n":"#21","p":1,"im":["0e3fb309127146f655f1c8192f166d823eb7eb18"],"m":21},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_22","t":"Hydra","a":"—","d":"","n":"#22","p":1,"im":["5fb45a2cb51fdbfba3dcc40c13d9521b02c03821","91a6b5b39386808401449562085c51e449a7884b"],"m":22},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_23","t":"Hydra","a":"—","d":"","n":"#23","p":1,"im":["a8ad033ad12f4565a3b415b8c90dc43f57768ee0"],"m":23},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_24","t":"Hydra","a":"—","d":"","n":"#24","p":1,"im":["67c74e01bda8ddad1dec995c873eef0ea4e4aee9"],"m":24},{"id":"flaglimitshydra_p1_25","t":"einrikr","a":"—","d":"","n":"#25","p":1,"im":["5b53a3488b07583694c916b722dc456b26d97b24"],"m":25}],"images":